    "name": "ti_z_x_large_share",
    "mechanism": "Informed-flow conditioning: the same net aggressive imbalance carries different information depending on the size distribution that produced it. Net buying imbalance assembled from a few large prints flags institutional/informed execution (information events do not get split to dust), while the same imbalance from many small retail prints is noise. Multiplying the 180s z-scored signed imbalance by the concurrent large-trade volume share up-weights the informed variant, which should continue at 15-60s horizons. This is the signed/conditioned repair of the direction-free large-trade level that died in iter-002.",
